+left.  Assume the jump \(M_t-M_{t-}\) is integrable.  Assume also that, almost
+surely, \(M\) is bounded by a deterministic constant \(C\) on the horizon
+\([\bot,t]\).  Then the deterministic jump at \(t\) vanishes:
+\[
+  M_t=M_{t-}
+\]
+almost surely.
+\end{lemma}
